questions.text:
Consider the following corpus:

&lt;s&gt; I am Sam &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; I like college &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Do Sam like college &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Sam I am &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Do I like Sam &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Do I like college &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; I do like Sam &lt;/s&gt;

List all possible bigrams. Compute conditional probabilities and predict the next word for: like, Sam

Consider the following corpus:

&lt;s&gt; Four students Ravi, Ramesh, Rekha and Rita are solving problems &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Ravi is solving math problems &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Ramesh is solving a logic puzzle &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Rekha is solving a hard problem &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Rita is solving a puzzle with patience &lt;/s&gt;

List all possible bigrams. Compute conditional probabilities and predict the next word for: solving, is

Consider the following corpus:

&lt;s&gt; I tell you to sleep and rest &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; I would like to sleep for an hour &lt;/s&gt;  
&lt;s&gt; Sleep helps one to relax &lt;/s&gt;

List all possible bigrams. Compute conditional probabilities and predict the next word for the word "to".
